  "notes": [
    "Every original upstream file is unchanged; git_blob_sha identifies the exact upstream Git object of its UTF-8 bytes. It is not a branch/commit. Verify Git blob SHA while materializing; no trailing newline is to be added.",
    "DCAT-AP3.0.1 full shapes and ranges are separate user-selected inputs. No hidden ontology union, automatic URL download or uncontrolled network import is prescribed.",
    "W3C shacl.ttl is the stable SHACL vocabulary file carrying its own2021-01-19 version notice and W3C2015 license. The historical shacl-shacl file identifies itself as a2017-04-04 draft validating a subset of syntax; use the maintained pySHACL meta_shacl runtime for validation.",
    "org.ttl explicitly declares the Open Data Commons PDDL1.0 license. dcat3.ttl explicitly declares CC-BY4.0. DCAT-AP repository LICENSE contains the full CC-BY4.0 text. Keep all original multilingual labels and metadata.",
    "W3C Software/Document2015 and2023 full notices, plus the Document2023 full notice, accompany the corresponding files. The W3C Document2023 terms expressly cover specification implementation derivatives and code components; no rebranding as an alternative W3C technical specification is intended.",
    "Original DCAT examples moved2026-09-18 from w3c/dxwg/dcat into w3c/dx-dcat/TR. These are the actual current retained file objects, not stale paths. Public CSIRO/Genoa examples are published reference metadata, not assertions of current source-endpoint availability.",
    "Graph examples include Turtle, JSON-LD and named-graph TriG. Preserve graph context, blank-node semantics, language tags, datatypes and source edition. The two basic-example serializations are independently published inputs; prove any equivalence through RDFLib rather than assuming textual correspondence.",
    "Neutral interoperability reference domain: this source package does not describe SAIC's unpublished customer ontology, award deliverables, actual systems or acceptance policy."
  ],
  "materialization": "Write each files[].content exactly as UTF-8 beneath an explicit selected source directory. Verify each non-null git_blob_sha as SHA1(b'blob '+str(len(bytes)).encode()+b'\\0'+bytes). Keep original files immutable; selected user corrections belong to separately named editions.",
